WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.837
Why now?

2
00:00:00.837 --> 00:00:04.050
Because two migrations
open one design window.

3
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:11.092
On the HR side: the December 10, 2025 memo
from OMB and OPM creates Federal HR 2.0,

4
00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:15.675
one government-wide core
human capital platform.

5
00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:19.951
OPM awarded the platform
contract on June 10, 2026,

6
00:00:19.951 --> 00:00:25.375
and the first agencies begin
moving as fiscal year 2027 starts.

7
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:29.036
The memo's sample timeline runs
about eight months per agency,

8
00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:32.912
with the agency's interconnections
going live around month five.

9
00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:38.623
On the identity side: agencies are moving
from Active Directory to Entra ID anyway,

10
00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:42.401
which is the Federal
Modernization Workbook's Book 02.

11
00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:47.312
In Entra ID, attributes drive Conditional
Access, groups and delegation,

12
00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:52.388
and inbound provisioning from an HR
system is a documented, supported path.

13
00:00:52.388 --> 00:00:53.538
So there's a window.

14
00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:57.042
The identity feed has to be
designed in during onboarding,

15
00:00:57.042 --> 00:01:00.838
before the interconnection goes
live, not bolted on afterward.

16
00:01:00.838 --> 00:01:06.162
One honest limit: Federal HR 2.0
covers federal employees only.

17
00:01:06.162 --> 00:01:09.877
Contractors and vendors need
their own authoritative source,

18
00:01:09.877 --> 00:01:13.010
and the onboarding is the
right time to decide it too.
